Assignment: Flowchart — User Input Validation
Objective:
Create a UiPath Flowchart that takes an input from the user, checks whether the input is a person's name, and displays the appropriate result.

Activities Used
Flowchart
Input Dialog
Assign
If
Message Box
Write Line

Steps
Step 1: Create a Flowchart
Create a new UiPath Process.
In the Designer Panel, add a Flowchart activity.
Use the Flowchart as the main structure of the automation.
Step 2: Take Input from the User
Use the Input Dialog activity to ask the user to enter a value.

Example:
Title: User Input
Label: Enter your name:
Store the entered value in a String variable:
userInput

Step 3: Check Whether the Input is a Person's Name
Use an If activity to check whether the entered value is a person's name.
For this assignment, we can consider the input to be a person's name if it contains only alphabetic characters.
Example condition:
System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex.IsMatch(userInput, "^[A-Za-z ]+$")
This checks whether the input contains only letters and spaces.

Step 4: If the Input is a Name
Connect the True branch of the If activity to a Message Box.
Display:
Name: [userInput]
For example, if the user enters:
Sanjana
The Message Box displays:
Name: Sanjana

Step 5: If the Input is Not a Name
Connect the False branch of the If activity to a Write Line activity.
Use Write Line to display the input in the Output Panel.
Example:
If the user enters:
12345
The Output Panel displays:
12345

Workflow Structure :

The final Flowchart can be arranged as:

                 Start
                   ↓
             Input Dialog
                   ↓
              User Input
                   ↓
             Check Input
                   ↓
             Is it a name?
              ↙         ↘
           Yes           No
            ↓             ↓
      Message Box      Write Line
      Display Name    Output Panel
Activities and Purpose
Activity	      Purpose
Flowchart	Controls the overall workflow
Input Dialog	Takes input from the user
If	Checks whether the input is a person's name
Message Box	Displays the name when the condition is True
Write Line	Displays the input in the Output Panel when the condition is False
Result

The automation successfully takes input from the user, validates the input, displays the name when the input is a valid person's name, and writes other inputs to the Output Panel.
